s","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","cmd-8b0e0b608ec1471a","cmd-6080eac50af54b7f","cmd-8b29669ab3ca4b60","cmd-056aa33701a04bcd"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes of the task — configuring minlen=12/minclass=3 on node1 and proving enforcement at the exact boundary — are satisfied with direct, high-quality evidence (config file content, PAM wiring, and live passwd attempts with shadow-hash verification at each boundary). The independent provider-wide restart protocol was also executed cleanly: baseline boot_id and healthy state were captured, the reboot ack returned before disconnect, the node was polled through the disruption, the boot_id changed (cce73776... to 29682ff7...) consistent with the fixed before/after lifecycle snapshots, and the policy file, PAM wiring, and enforcement behavior were all re-confirmed post-reboot. Minor hygiene issues are limited to a handful of leftover diagnostic log files in /tmp and one redundant test re-run; none affected task functionality or system security.","limitations":["Restart/reboot was not itself required by the public task contract (a static password-complexity policy change); its evidence is assessed only as the separately-mandated node-restart protocol and does not affect the task's satisfied status.","Leftover /tmp diagnostic log files (out1-8.log, reboot.log) were not cleaned up, though they pose negligible risk and contain no secrets beyond command output already visible in the trace.","Cluster-state recovery is not applicable since node1 is a single unclustered node in this topology."]},"ttft_ms":16386,"type":"result","duration_ms":43875,"uuid":"6c032166-9643-413e-9d8c-7fc067a79938","ttft_stream_ms":1136,"time_to_request_ms":240,"first_content_frame_ms":1136,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
